{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, thanks for reporting this. I checked your mailbox and there is no quarantined message from the meeting, so it was not caught by spam filtering. To narrow this down, please reply with: 1) the name of the person who sent the Q4 planning invite and roughly when it went out, 2) whether the invite shows up when you open Outlook on the web (outlook.office.com) in a browser, and 3) whether an assistant or anyone else manages your calendar or receives invites on your behalf. Also, your work laptop has not checked in with our systems for about 12 days, so if you have been working on it, please let us know and restart it while connected to the office network or VPN. Once we have these details we can ask the organizer to resend the invite or escalate further.",
  "internal_note": "Checked: account sofia.rossi (user_id 7) is active, not locked, no failed logins, mailbox 27.9% used, VPN enabled. Spam quarantine is empty, so KB-012 step 1 is ruled out and no release is needed. Device BL-LT-0107 is offline with no check-in for 12 days, which could affect desktop sync (KB-009), but it does not explain a missing invite on its own. Not yet verified: delegate or assistant settings (no tool available to read them), whether OWA shows the invite, and who the organizer is. Next steps once the user replies: confirm OWA view, check delegate setup, and have the organizer resend. If the invite never arrives from one specific internal sender, escalate to Tier 2 per KB-012 (possible mail rule or transport issue). No actions were queued.",
